# [CompliRules] Multi-Jurisdiction Collision Resolution: GDPR Erasure vs Statutory Tax/Clinical Retentions
**Severity:** `CRITICAL` | **Jurisdiction:** `GDPR_EU`

<!-- NOTICE: CompliRules provides automated AST guardrails under MIT License without warranty (See DISCLAIMER.md). Documentation: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/ -->

## Legal Citations
- **Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) (Article 17(3)(b) & Article 18)**: Right to erasure does not apply to the extent processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation.
- **Turkish Tax Procedure Law & Commercial Code (VUK Madde 253 & TTK Madde 82)**: Mandatory 5-year (VUK) and 10-year (TTK) retention of accounting books and invoice records.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: Never execute hard SQL cascade deletes on invoices, tax records, or medical charts upon user erasure requests.
- MUST: Quarantine retained financial and clinical rows into restricted, read-only tables.
- MUST: Attach automated TTL destruction timers matching exact statutory retention durations.

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: Hard CASCADE deletion between User and Invoice/Billing tables

